        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "72155a1d-f1ca-51f5-90c0-1b25833d4ffb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dmitri Usatov, Antonín Dvořák, Adolf Čech, Karel Kovařovic, Jindřich Kaftan\n- Works: The Devil and Kate\n- Roles: singer, composer, conductor, répétiteur, arranger\n- Concepts: friends and collaborators of a composer\n\nFacts:\n- Dmitri Usatov sang roles in operas, but this chunk identifies The Devil and Kate as the work with more contributions from friends of its composer.\n- Antonín Dvořák composed The Devil and Kate.\n- Adolf Čech, a friend of Antonín Dvořák, conducted the premiere of The Devil and Kate.\n- Karel Kovařovic, another friend of Antonín Dvořák, served as répétiteur for The Devil and Kate.\n- Jindřich Kaftan, also a friend of Antonín Dvořák, arranged The Devil and Kate for piano duet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
